PARAMETER-SPACE SCAN v2 -- relativistic-MOND architectures vs the full gate battery
============================================================================================================
  cores = 16;  a0 footings = {'canonical': 9.3619e-11, 'alt': 1.13e-10};  CMB gate = Planck omega_c (default)

============================================================================================================
PART 0 -- CONTROLS.  Do the gates reproduce the results they claim to encode?
============================================================================================================
  [PASS] C1a  the two-piece alpha_1 reduces to the banked -2(K_B+2) at c14 = K_B, J_Y = 1   (alpha_1(c14=K_B=0.1, J_Y=1) = -4.2000 = -2(K_B+2))
  [PASS] C1b  min |alpha_1| over the physical AeST box reproduces L91's control 2.333   (min|alpha_1| = 2.3333  (2.3e+04x the bound))
  [PASS] C2  the relic N_eff floor reproduces g04i's 27.6 eV from first principles here (Omega_x h^2 = (m/93.14) r^3, Delta N_eff = r^4 <= 0.3)   (r_max = 0.7401, m_floor = 27.57 eV  (g04i: 27.6 eV))
  [PASS] C3  baryon-only z_eq < z_rec, and the full Planck cold density puts z_eq well above it   (z_eq(baryons only) = 535;  z_eq(omega_c = 0.12) = 3406; z_rec = 1090)
  [PASS] C4  L126's two horns reproduce: a galaxy-tuned graviton mass kills the CMB, a CMB-tuned one leaves galaxies fully transmitting   (Compton 7 kpc -> eta(CMB) = 2.27e-09;  Compton 276 Mpc -> eta(gal) = 1.000000; 4.6 decades apart)

  C5  MUTATION CONTROLS (the anti-manufactured-no-go test).  Each control switches OFF one
      gate and asks whether a survivor appears.  If nothing ever survives, the battery is
      broken; if the right thing survives, the gate is load-bearing and correctly aimed.
  [PASS] C5a  switching OFF the galaxy-smoothness gate resuscitates the cold-dark-matter hybrid (so G8 is what kills it, and the rest of the battery does admit a solution)   (16 architectures survive without G8; dark sectors = ['particle_CDM', 'thermal_relic'])
  [PASS] C5b  switching OFF causality + the deep-MOND gradient instability lets the PROPAGATING branch back in (so G1/G15 are load-bearing, not decorative)   (48 architectures survive; carriers = ['cuscuton', 'propagating'])
  [PASS] C5c  with EVERY gate on, the survivor set is empty -- and (by C5a/C5b) that emptiness is produced by identifiable gates, not by a battery that rejects everything   (0 survivors with the full battery)

============================================================================================================
PART 1 -- GATE AUDIT.  Three corrections, each verified in both directions.
============================================================================================================

  A1  RAQUAL CAUSALITY -- the gate is right, its stated REASON was not.
      L120/L106 quote c_s^2 = 1/(2n-1), superluminal for 1/2 < n < 1, and assert the
      MOND->Newton transition passes through that band.  Computed from the kernels:
        exp        n_eff in [1.0000, 1.4975]   enters (1/2,1)? False   max c_par^2 = 1.9950   max c_timelike^2 = 1.0000
        simple     n_eff in [1.0050, 1.4950]   enters (1/2,1)? False   max c_par^2 = 1.9901   max c_timelike^2 = 0.9902
        standard   n_eff in [1.0001, 1.4999]   enters (1/2,1)? False   max c_par^2 = 1.9999   max c_timelike^2 = 0.9999
        nu_RAR     n_eff in [1.0001, 1.4950]   enters (1/2,1)? False   max c_par^2 = 1.9901   max c_timelike^2 = 0.9998
  [PASS] A1a  CORRECTION: no standard kernel ever enters L120's quoted band 1/2 < n < 1. A monotone mu forces n_eff in [1, 3/2], so the gate's STATED reason never fires   (all four kernels keep n_eff >= 1 (deep MOND n = 3/2, Newtonian n = 1, monotone between))
  [PASS] A1b  the gate is nevertheless CORRECT on the right calculation: for a SPACELIKE background gradient (the quasi-static galactic problem) the longitudinal characteristic is c_par^2 = 2n-1, which is > 1 for every n > 1, i.e. throughout the MOND regime   (max c_par^2 = exp:1.995, simple:1.990, standard:2.000, nu_RAR:1.990  (deep MOND n=3/2 -> c_par^2 = 2, the classic Bekenstein-Milgrom acausality))
  [PASS] A1c  the two quoted speeds are reciprocals over the whole grid, so both are right in their own regime: 1/(2n-1) is the TIMELIKE (cosmological phi(t)) k-essence sound speed, 2n-1 the SPACELIKE (quasi-static) longitudinal characteristic; the galactic problem is the spacelike one, and it gives the classic c^2 = 2 in deep MOND   (c_par^2 * c_timelike^2 = 1 to 1e-10 on all four kernels; deep-MOND n_eff = 1.4995 => c_par^2 = 1.999)

  A2  VELOCITY-ORDERING LEMMA -- true as a monotonicity statement, INSUFFICIENT as a closure.
  [PASS] A2a  the lemma's monotonicity is confirmed: for a decoupled species with v_rms ~ 1/a the comoving Jeans wavenumber k_J ~ sqrt(a) is strictly increasing (matter domination)   (k_J(a) strictly increasing on a in [1e-4, 1]; k_J ~ a^0.5)
  [PASS] A2b  CORRECTION: the growth from recombination to today is sqrt(1091) = 33, NOT 1091 (L125's 'k_fs ~ a' drops the sqrt(rho) factor). And 33 is SMALLER than the CMB-to-galaxy scale gap of 333, so the lemma ALONE leaves a ~1 decade window open   (k_J growth rec->now = 33.0x; required scale gap k_gal/k_peak3 = 333x; open window = 1.00 dex in comoving velocity)
        linear-Jeans window on the comoving velocity u = a*v_rms: [2.32, 23.39] km/s  -- NOT empty
        escape-speed criterion instead: u >= v_esc = 300 km/s vs the same CMB ceiling 23.4 km/s  -- empty by 1.11 dex
  [PASS] A2c  the closure comes from the PHASE-SPACE / escape criterion, not from the lemma: a species cold enough for the CMB has v_rms today far below galactic escape speeds, so it is captured by the baryonic well regardless of where its linear Jeans scale sits   (v_esc/u_max(CMB) = 13x  => bound, hence present in galaxies)
        independent Tremaine-Gunn cross-check of the CITED 11.4 eV RAR ceiling: the phase-space floor is 25 eV (MW-like) to 198 eV (dwarf-like)
  [PASS] A2d  HONEST FLAG: this script reproduces the relic pincer's N_eff arm exactly (27.6 eV) but CANNOT reproduce the 11.4 eV RAR arm from first principles; an independent Tremaine-Gunn estimate BRACKETS rather than confirms it. G10 is the weakest gate   (TG bracket [25, 198] eV straddles the 27.6 eV floor; the CITED ceiling 11.4 eV sits below the bracket)

  A3  COLD-FRACTION CONTINUUM -- the old binary gate hid the real margin.
        canonical footing: galaxy ceiling f <= 0.582;  CMB floor f >= 0.193 (z_eq only) or f >= 0.970 (Planck omega_c, 3 sigma)
                    -> z_eq-only gate leaves the window f in [0.193, 0.582] (NON-EMPTY);  Planck gate closes it by 0.222 dex = 42 sigma on omega_c
        alt       footing: galaxy ceiling f <= 0.486;  CMB floor f >= 0.193 (z_eq only) or f >= 0.970 (Planck omega_c, 3 sigma)
                    -> z_eq-only gate leaves the window f in [0.193, 0.486] (NON-EMPTY);  Planck gate closes it by 0.300 dex = 51 sigma on omega_c
  [PASS] A3a  CORRECTION: the CMB gate must be quoted with its strength. Under the weakest possible reading (z_eq > z_rec only) a partial-cold-matter window is OPEN; it is closed only by Planck's omega_c measurement   (z_eq floor 0.193 < ceiling 0.582 < Planck floor 0.970)
  [PASS] A3b  the closure is therefore a 0.22 dex pincer, not an infinite one -- and it is the TIGHTEST gap anywhere in the enumeration   (canonical 0.222 dex / alt 0.300 dex)

  A4  REGRESSION TEST for the old spurious sterile-neutrino survivor.
      The previous bug: G-gal EXEMPTED a keV 'cold sterile neutrino' on the story that it
      free-streams out of galaxies while clustering on large scales.  That is false -- a keV
      relic has v_rms today of order metres per second and forms galaxy halos.  Verified:
        m =     1000 eV supplying omega_c needs T_x/T_nu = 0.2236; v_rms today = 3.541e-02 km/s  (escape speed ~ 300 km/s)
        m =    10000 eV supplying omega_c needs T_x/T_nu = 0.1038; v_rms today = 1.644e-03 km/s  (escape speed ~ 300 km/s)
  [PASS] A4  no exemption survives: a keV relic that supplies omega_c is ~7 orders of magnitude below galactic escape speeds, so it clusters in galaxies and must face G8 like any CDM. The current battery grants NO dark sector a free pass on G8   (v_rms(keV relic today) = 3.541e+01 m/s = 1.18e-04 x v_esc)
  [PASS] A4b  and the converse over-strictness check: G8 is NOT applied to sectors that supply no clustering density (they fail G7 instead), nor to relics below the CITED RAR ceiling   (G8 fires only when eta_eff * f exceeds the ceiling; eta_eff = 0 below 11.4 eV)

